  "notes": "カット is a very common loanword from English \"cut,\" used both as a noun and as a suru verb (カット⟦する→する：00392_suru⟧).\n\nSENSE 1 — HAIRCUT:\nAt hair salons, カット refers specifically to the cutting service. Pricing menus typically list カット separately from other services.\n\nSENSE 2 — DELETION/REDUCTION:\nUsed in film editing, business cost-cutting, and general removal of content.\n\nCOMPOUNDS:\n- ヘアカット: haircut\n- コストカット: cost cutting\n- ⟦{賃金|ちんぎん}→賃金：04842_chingin⟧カット: wage cut\n- カット⟦{野菜|やさい}→野菜：02265_yasai⟧: pre-cut vegetables",
